@* Theming (UI docs): light and dark, the theme switch, re-theming a subtree, and every design token. *@

<p>Every colour, size and effect of the components is a <code>--dnf-*</code> custom property in
    <code>src/DotNetForge.UI/Styles/tokens.css</code>. Components use the semantic tokens only, never literal values, so
    re-theming is overriding tokens - for the whole page or for any part of it. Tailwind utilities read the same tokens
    (<a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/customization#level-2">Customization</a>), so they follow too.</p>

<h2 id="light-and-dark">Light and dark</h2>
<ul>
    <li><code>:root</code> declares <code>color-scheme: light dark</code>, and every colour token is
        <code>light-dark(light, dark)</code>: the browser picks the value from the element's <strong>effective</strong>
        colour scheme. Components never test the theme.</li>
    <li>Without a choice, the system preference (<code>prefers-color-scheme</code>) applies.</li>
    <li><code>data-theme="light"</code> or <code>data-theme="dark"</code> sets <code>color-scheme</code> on its element - on
        <code>&lt;html&gt;</code> for the whole page, or <strong>on any subtree</strong> to force one theme there.</li>
    <li>Tailwind's <code>dark:</code> variant agrees: it applies inside <code>data-theme="dark"</code> and, with a dark
        system preference, everywhere except inside <code>data-theme="light"</code>. A logo pair uses it:
        <code>&lt;img class="block dark:hidden"&gt;</code> plus <code>&lt;img class="hidden dark:block"&gt;</code>.</li>
</ul>

<ui-doc-example id="subtree-themes" title="Themes on a subtree" description="The first card is always light and the second always dark, whatever the page's theme. The third follows the page and re-themes itself: it is a dnf-scope that overrides the primary colour." layout="block">
    <div class="dnf-grid dnf-grid--cols-3">
        <div class="dnf-card" data-theme="light">
            <div class="dnf-card__body dnf-stack">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold">Always light</p>
                <div class="dnf-cluster">
                    <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--primary">Publish</button>
                    <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--secondary">Preview</button>
                </div>
                <input class="dnf-input" aria-label="Page title, light card" value="About us" />
                <label class="dnf-switch-row"><span class="dnf-check__text">Show in menu</span><input type="checkbox" role="switch" class="dnf-switch" checked /></label>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="dnf-card" data-theme="dark">
            <div class="dnf-card__body dnf-stack">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold">Always dark</p>
                <div class="dnf-cluster">
                    <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--primary">Publish</button>
                    <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--secondary">Preview</button>
                </div>
                <input class="dnf-input" aria-label="Page title, dark card" value="About us" />
                <label class="dnf-switch-row"><span class="dnf-check__text">Show in menu</span><input type="checkbox" role="switch" class="dnf-switch" checked /></label>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="dnf-card dnf-scope dnf-docs-demo-brand">
            <div class="dnf-card__body dnf-stack">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold">Re-themed scope</p>
                <div class="dnf-cluster">
                    <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--primary">Publish</button>
                    <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--secondary">Preview</button>
                </div>
                <input class="dnf-input" aria-label="Page title, re-themed card" value="About us" />
                <label class="dnf-switch-row"><span class="dnf-check__text">Show in menu</span><input type="checkbox" role="switch" class="dnf-switch" checked /></label>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</ui-doc-example>

<p>The third card's rule, in the docs' own stylesheet (unlayered):</p>

<ui-doc-code id="subtree-brand-css" lang="css">
.dnf-docs-demo-brand {
    --dnf-primary: #7c3aed;
    --dnf-primary-foreground: #ffffff;
    --dnf-primary-text: light-dark(#6d28d9, #c4b5fd);
}
</ui-doc-code>

<h2 id="switching">Switching the theme</h2>
<p>The user's choice is stored in <code>localStorage</code> under <code>dnf-theme</code> (<code>light</code> or
    <code>dark</code>; no entry means the system preference). Two scripts share it:</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong><code>dnf-theme.js</code></strong> - loaded synchronously in <code>&lt;head&gt;</code>, before the stylesheet.
        It sets <code>&lt;html data-theme&gt;</code> from <code>dnf-theme</code> before the first paint (no flash) and adds
        the class <code>dnf-js</code> to <code>&lt;html&gt;</code>, so <code>dnf-js-only</code> elements such as the theme
        menu show from the first paint. Blocked storage falls back to the system preference.</li>
    <li><strong><code>dnf.js</code></strong> - any element with <code>data-theme-set="light|dark|system"</code> switches on
        click: it sets or removes <code>data-theme</code> on <code>&lt;html&gt;</code>, stores or clears
        <code>dnf-theme</code>, and sets <code>aria-checked="true"</code> on the matching <code>[data-theme-set]</code>
        elements (<code>"false"</code> on the others).</li>
</ul>
<p>Every page that loads <code>dnf-theme.js</code> shares the choice: the admin, the sign-in screens, these docs and the
    admin tabs of extensions.</p>

<ui-doc-example id="theme-switch" title="A theme switch" description="Menu items with data-theme-set switch this whole page; the checked one shows a check mark.">
    <dnf-dropdown text="Theme" label="Colour theme" variant="Secondary" size="Md" placement="bottom-start">
        <dnf-dropdown-button icon="sun" role="menuitemradio" aria-checked="false" data-theme-set="light">Light</dnf-dropdown-button>
        <dnf-dropdown-button icon="moon" role="menuitemradio" aria-checked="false" data-theme-set="dark">Dark</dnf-dropdown-button>
        <dnf-dropdown-button icon="monitor" role="menuitemradio" aria-checked="false" data-theme-set="system">System</dnf-dropdown-button>
    </dnf-dropdown>
</ui-doc-example>

<p>The CMS's theme menu (<code>Views/Shared/_ThemeMenu.cshtml</code>, in the admin top bar and the header of these
    docs) is an icon button whose sun or moon follows the effective theme through <code>dark:</code>. It is
    <code>dnf-js-only</code>, because without JavaScript there is nothing to switch:</p>

<ui-doc-code id="theme-menu-markup" lang="razor">
<div class="dnf-dropdown dnf-js-only">
    <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--ghost dnf-button--icon-only" popovertarget="theme-menu" aria-haspopup="menu"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Colour theme">
        <dnf-icon name="sun" class="inline dark:hidden" />
        <dnf-icon name="moon" class="hidden dark:inline" />
    </button>
    <div class="dnf-dropdown__menu" id="theme-menu" popover role="menu" aria-label="Colour theme" data-placement="bottom-end">
        <dnf-dropdown-label>Theme</dnf-dropdown-label>
        <dnf-dropdown-button icon="sun" role="menuitemradio" aria-checked="false" data-theme-set="light">Light</dnf-dropdown-button>
        <dnf-dropdown-button icon="moon" role="menuitemradio" aria-checked="false" data-theme-set="dark">Dark</dnf-dropdown-button>
        <dnf-dropdown-button icon="monitor" role="menuitemradio" aria-checked="false" data-theme-set="system">System</dnf-dropdown-button>
    </div>
</div>
</ui-doc-code>

<h2 id="subtrees">Re-theming a subtree</h2>
<p>Override <strong>leaf</strong> tokens on an element, in your own unlayered CSS. Mark the element
    <code>dnf-scope</code> when you override a colour that has derived tokens, so its hover and soft shades follow:</p>

<ui-doc-code id="subtree-css" lang="css">
.reports.dnf-scope {
    --dnf-primary: #2563eb;            /* hover, soft and soft-border follow (derived) */
    --dnf-primary-foreground: #ffffff;
    --dnf-primary-text: light-dark(#1d4ed8, #93c5fd);
    --dnf-radius-md: 2px;
}
</ui-doc-code>

<p>Everything inside follows - components and Tailwind utilities (<code>bg-primary</code>, <code>rounded-md</code>) alike,
    because both read the tokens through <code>var()</code>. Keep a light and a dark value with <code>light-dark()</code>.
    An extension's root element is a scope (<a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/extensions#isolation">Extensions</a>).</p>

<h3 id="derived">Derived tokens</h3>
<p>Computed from the leaves with <code>color-mix()</code>, on <code>:root</code> <strong>and on every
    <code>.dnf-scope</code></strong>. A custom property is computed where it is declared, so a derived token declared
    only on <code>:root</code> would keep the root's primary colour inside an element that overrides it; declaring it
    again on <code>.dnf-scope</code> fixes that.</p>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Token</th><th>Swatch</th><th>From</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>--dnf-primary-hover</code></td><td>-</td><td><code>--dnf-primary</code> mixed with 8% black</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>--dnf-primary-soft</code>, <code>--dnf-primary-soft-border</code></td><td><span class="inline-block size-4 rounded-sm border border-border-strong align-middle bg-primary-soft" aria-hidden="true"></span></td><td><code>--dnf-primary</code> tinted (light) or translucent (dark)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>--dnf-success-soft</code></td><td><span class="inline-block size-4 rounded-sm border border-border-strong align-middle bg-success-soft" aria-hidden="true"></span></td><td><code>--dnf-success</code>, tinted or translucent</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>--dnf-warning-soft</code></td><td><span class="inline-block size-4 rounded-sm border border-border-strong align-middle bg-warning-soft" aria-hidden="true"></span></td><td><code>--dnf-warning</code>, tinted or translucent</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>--dnf-danger-soft</code></td><td><span class="inline-block size-4 rounded-sm border border-border-strong align-middle bg-danger-soft" aria-hidden="true"></span></td><td><code>--dnf-danger</code>, tinted or translucent</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>--dnf-info-soft</code></td><td><span class="inline-block size-4 rounded-sm border border-border-strong align-middle bg-info-soft" aria-hidden="true"></span></td><td><code>--dnf-info</code>, tinted or translucent</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>--dnf-danger-hover</code></td><td>-</td><td><code>--dnf-danger</code> 12% darker (light) or lighter (dark)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>--dnf-focus-ring</code></td><td>-</td><td><code>0 0 0 2px var(--dnf-surface), 0 0 0 4px var(--dnf-focus)</code> - a <code>box-shadow</code></td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 id="tokens">Tokens</h2>

