<h3 id="stacking">Stacking</h3>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Token</th><th>Value</th><th>Used by</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>--dnf-z-sticky</code></td><td>10</td><td>the CMS admin shell</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>--dnf-z-drawer</code></td><td>40</td><td>the CMS admin shell</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>--dnf-z-dialog</code></td><td>50</td><td>nothing in the library - dialogs use the top layer</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>--dnf-z-toast</code></td><td>60</td><td><code>dnf-toast-region</code>, <code>dnf-skip-link</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>--dnf-z-tooltip</code></td><td>70</td><td><code>dnf-tooltip</code></td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
<p>Dropdowns, popovers, dialogs and the tooltip open in the browser's top layer, where <code>z-index</code> does not
    apply (<a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/extensions#overlays">overlays</a>).</p>

<h2 id="contrast">Contrast</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Every other text token meets WCAG 2.2 AA (at least 4.5:1) on <code>--dnf-surface</code> and
        <code>--dnf-background</code> in both themes.</li>
    <li>Orange is a <strong>fill</strong> colour with <strong>white</strong> on top (<code>--dnf-primary-foreground</code>,
        3.0:1) - the brand's choice, below AA for small text. For a fill that passes with white, override
        <code>--dnf-primary</code> (for example <code>#cc4a0a</code>, 4.6:1). Orange <strong>text</strong> uses
        <code>--dnf-primary-text</code> (5.2:1 light, 8.4:1 dark).</li>
    <li>Never use <code>--dnf-forge-500</code> for text, and check contrast again when you
        add or override a colour token.</li>
</ul>
